  "TITLE": "The Network Effect:<br>Why Bigger Gets Better",
  "LEAD": "A network's value doesn't grow with its users &mdash; it grows with the connections between them, which increase roughly with the square of the user count (Metcalfe's Law): 2 users support 1 possible link, but 6 users support 15. It's the same reason a shared plant utility &mdash; a steam header, a flare system, a site-wide historian &mdash; gets more valuable every time another unit ties into it: each new tie-in multiplies the exchanges the network can support, not just adds one more user.",
